From: grislux55 <jebchou.hg@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: enable the factory QDMA QoS aging policy

The AN7581 factory qdma_lan.ko and qdma_wan.ko both call
qdma_dev_aging_init() during QDMA setup. The function sets the QoS aging
enable and fast-replacement bits, clears the aging-method bit for threshold
mode, and preserves the aging time and unrelated fields.

Program the same fields after the existing QDMA QoS initialization on each
controller. A read-modify-write preserves the time setting and the other
QDMA state initialized by the driver.

The bit layout was checked against the independent public SDK functions
qdmaEnableQosAgingEn(), qdmaSetQosAgingMethod() and
qdmaEnableQosAgingFastReplaceEn(). The factory machine code performs the
same three updates at QDMA_CSR_QOS_AGING_CFG (0x10bc).

Factory modules: XG-040G-MD 7.3.160.1_v002, qdma_lan.ko SHA256
337d66fca6bef01d7e83f1d441e10585825816d61b15614efbde09cdd0a6d9c8 and
qdma_wan.ko SHA256
29713c102f67e71681b850e0aac387aacbaa734a7bc1058447d682f5a9eb23c8.
SDK register/API reference: lotusmomo/airoha_sdk at
32b5aa356c2406edef8806aaf75451ff0a5286f2,
private/qdma/qdma_lan/{qdma_dev_7581.h,qdma_dev.c}.

Signed-off-by: grislux55 <jebchou.hg@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -1905,6 +1905,12 @@ static void airoha_qdma_init_qos(struct a
 	airoha_qdma_clear(qdma, REG_PSE_BUF_USAGE_CFG,
 			  PSE_BUF_ESTIMATE_EN_MASK);
 
+	/* Use the factory aging policy: threshold, fast replacement, enabled. */
+	airoha_qdma_rmw(qdma, REG_QOS_AGING_CFG,
+			QOS_AGING_EN_MASK | QOS_AGING_METHOD_MASK |
+			QOS_AGING_FAST_REPLACE_MASK,
+			QOS_AGING_EN_MASK | QOS_AGING_FAST_REPLACE_MASK);
+
 	airoha_qdma_set(qdma, REG_EGRESS_RATE_METER_CFG,
 			EGRESS_RATE_METER_EN_MASK |
 			EGRESS_RATE_METER_EQ_RATE_EN_MASK);
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_regs.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_regs.h
@@ -869,6 +869,11 @@
 #define TXQ_CNGST_TIME_TRIGGER		BIT(16)
 #define TXQ_CNGST_TICKSEL_MASK		GENMASK(15, 0)
 
+#define REG_QOS_AGING_CFG		0x10bc
+#define QOS_AGING_EN_MASK		BIT(31)
+#define QOS_AGING_METHOD_MASK		BIT(30)
+#define QOS_AGING_FAST_REPLACE_MASK	BIT(29)
+
 /* Dynamic bounds: total, channel and queue. */
 #define REG_TXQ_DYN_THR(_n)		(0x10a4 + ((_n) << 2))
 #define REG_TXQ_DEI_THR(_n)		(0x10d4 + ((_n) << 2))
